      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "MR. CHIVES (6) goes very well this trip starting 11 times for four wins and three minors. Scored by 1.5 lengths last time (16.85) in a Grade 5 over 300m at this track. Looks suited and should go close. NEBULA BALE (5) rocketed out of the boxes with a strong early sectional but gathered in and finished in the minors when third (19.47) at this track over 350m. Form from her last run is proving strong. Hard to beat again. MORAINE PIPER (1) was out of the placings last time when sixth at Bendigo (24.24) but scored five back at Warragul (26.52). One of the better hopes. BRUREE PAT (7) is in the mix despite finishing out of the placings here last start. Something for the Multiples: MR. CHIVES (6)",
